1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:10,475
Most of the cloud runs on Linux, and servers have no screen. You talk to them by typing, like a skilled driver with a manual gearbox.

2
00:00:11,170 --> 00:00:18,245
Logs live in var log. Tail dash f follows new lines live, and grep finds words.

3
00:00:19,950 --> 00:00:27,875
Every file has an owner, and permissions to read, write and run, for the owner, the group and everyone else.

4
00:00:28,580 --> 00:00:36,605
Secrets should be readable only by the app's user. Never fix a problem with chmod seven seven seven.

5
00:00:38,300 --> 00:00:46,650
Use SSH keys, not passwords, and sudo only when needed, like a master key you return after use.

6
00:00:47,350 --> 00:00:51,275
And check the path twice before you delete anything.

